## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical I/O scheduling knowledge, correctness, and minimal code for a common OS component.

## Key Concepts
- SCAN elevator algorithm
- Head movement and direction reversal
- Service order derivation from a head position
- Edge cases: empty queue, all requests on one side

## Code Example
```c
// toy SCAN scheduler (upward)
int scan_schedule(int head, int req[], int n, int out[]) {
  int up[n], dn[n], upn=0, dnn=0, k=0;
  for (int i=0;i<n;i++) if (req[i] >= head) up[upn++] = req[i]; else dn[dnn++] = req[i];
  qsort(up, upn, sizeof(int), cmp_asc);
  qsort(dn, dnn, sizeof(int), cmp_desc);
  for (int i=0;i<upn;i++) out[k++] = up[i];
  for (int i=0;i<dnn;i++) out[k++] = dn[i];
  return k; // number of entries
}
```

